From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 04:00:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Log host memory by memory type, mapping and purpose in the
 census

The opt-in allocation census (rtx.profiler.memory.requestSnapshot) also writes
[RTX Host Memory] rows, with or without the memory profiler: every memory
type's chunks and dedicated allocations with their used bytes, the address
range of each host-visible memory object, the process counters, and the
committed address space by type and protection with the part DXVK's mappings
cover. Allocation groups gain the memory type flags the allocation received,
whether the application released the image while the renderer holds it, and
the allocation's name (its purpose).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
